  "published": "2026-10-02T10:38:13.79Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "9.2.0 - The delimited reader named the record before the one that went wrong: a record it could not read, and a record no schema matched, were both reported with the previous record's number, text and values. Only the first record in a file was ever named correctly. FixedLengthRecordReadEventArgs.RecordContext is new, so a handler for a record being read can see which record it is. A schema selector can now be told to pass a record over with When( predicate ).Skip(), which decides the same way in both readers - a handler for the record being read cannot, because the two raise that event on opposite sides of choosing a schema. DelimitedReader.ParseRecord splits one record's text into its values for a caller who has the text already. No breaking changes.",
